# characterization baseline: 26-empty-as-field-strands-multiconnector-frame
# On multi-connector hardware an empty `as` field yields an empty-string per-connector meter value, which MySQL strict mode rejects for the INT column -- throwing and stranding the frame. Only reachable once per-connector charge_points rows exist, so known issue 1 currently masks it. Found by the property suite (seed 20260907).
# documents: docs/known-issues.md#15-an-empty-as-field-strands-multi-connector-frames, tests/property/README.md#what-it-found
#
# Masked values: <CLOCK> clock-derived datetime, <TOKEN> in-flight
# claim token, [PID] worker process id.

